msgid ":issue:`1989`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:296
msgid "`1.16.3 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.3>`_ - 2026-07-26"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:301
msgid ""
"Allow read-only global list commands when venv lock files are inaccessible. "
"(:issue:`1974`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:307
msgid ""
"Direct Linux users to PEP 668-compatible installation methods. (:issue:"
"`1976`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:311
msgid "`1.16.2 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.2>`_ - 2026-07-21"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:316
msgid ""
"Stop venv inspection from crashing on Python 3.15 when a `dist-info` "
"directory has no `Name` metadata field. `importlib.metadata` now raises "
"`KeyError` for missing metadata keys instead of returning `None`; such "
"distributions are skipped again, as on earlier Python versions. (:issue:"
"`1971`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:322
msgid "`1.16.1 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.1>`_ - 2026-07-20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:327
msgid ""
"Stop `install` and `list` from crashing when the pipx bin directory contains "
"an executable pipx did not create. Scanning for launcher ownership decoded "
"arbitrary binary content as an interpreter path, which raised "
"`UnicodeDecodeError` on Windows, or `ValueError` for a path holding a NUL "
"byte. Such a file is now treated as not owned by the venv. (:issue:`1965`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:333
msgid "`1.16.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.0>`_ - 2026-07-15"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:338
msgid "Add `pipx list --outdated` and JSON output. (:issue:`149`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:339
msgid ""
"Honour the `requires-python` a package declares. When the default "
"interpreter fails it, pipx looks for one on the system that satisfies it and "
"builds the environment there, so `pipx install mytool` no longer needs the "
"user to work out the right `--python`. Pass `--fetch-python=missing` to let "
"pipx download a matching interpreter when the system carries none, and name "
"`--python` yourself to keep the last word. (:issue:`387`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:343
msgid "Normalize inferred `pipx run` package names. (:issue:`618`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:344
msgid "Allow `pipx list` to select installed packages by name. (:issue:`640`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:345
msgid "Add `--output` to structured commands. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:346
msgid ""
"Freeze the structured result envelope at `pipx_result_version` 1. Every `--"
"output json` document now carries the command as a list of CLI tokens, a "
"`status` of `success`, `partial`, or `error`, the process `exit_code`, the "
"command `data`, and a top-level `errors` list whose entries each have a "
"stable `code` and `message` alongside the `environment` and `package` they "
"concern. A failure that stops a command before it builds a result renders "
"the same envelope. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:350
msgid "Add quiet and JSON output for package maintenance. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:351
msgid ""
"Give `pipx reinstall` and `pipx reinstall-all` the structured output the "
"other commands carry. They printed straight to the terminal, so `--quiet` "
"left `uninstalled NAME!` behind and no `--output json` existed to read the "
"result from a script. Both now report through the shared renderer. (:issue:"
"`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:354
msgid ""
"Give `pipx cache`, `pipx interpreter`, `pipx upgrade-shared`, `pipx manifest "
"lock` and `pipx manifest sync` the structured output the other commands "
"carry, so `--quiet` silences them and `--output json` hands a script the "
"result. The `cache` and `interpreter` subcommands take `--quiet` and `--"
"verbose` for the first time, since the shared options had passed them by. "
"`pipx ensurepath` goes on printing its guidance, because its job is to tell "
"a person what to add to a shell profile. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:359
msgid ""
"Add `--output json` to `pipx inject` and `pipx uninject`. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:360
msgid "Infer the app name when running packages from VCS URLs. (:issue:`854`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:361
msgid "Stream installer output during verbose installs. (:issue:`1069`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:362
msgid ""
"Draw the download progress bar of `pip` and `uv` during a plain `pipx "
"install`, in place of the pipx spinner. pipx hands the installer a pseudo-"
"terminal, which is the only way `uv` reports progress, and asks `uv` for its "
"default output rather than the quiet one. A redirected stream keeps the "
"previous behaviour. (:issue:`1069`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:365
msgid "Allow commands to skip shared-library maintenance. (:issue:`1278`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:366
msgid "Install PEP 723 scripts as persistent applications. (:issue:`1388`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:367
msgid ""
"Point library install errors to `inject` and `--preinstall`. (:issue:`1411`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:368
msgid ""
"Add commands to diagnose and repair broken environment interpreters. (:issue:"
"`1442`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:369
msgid ""
"Add explicit tool manifests with separate PEP 751 locks. (:issue:`1506`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:370
msgid ""
"Add `pipx install --upgrade` to reconcile apps with package specs. (:issue:"
"`1572`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:371
msgid ""
"Expose the shell completion scripts a package ships, the way pipx already "
"exposes its man pages. A wheel that installs into `share/bash-completion/"
"completions`, `share/zsh/site-functions` or `share/fish/vendor_completions."
"d` gets those files linked under `PIPX_COMPLETION_DIR`, which defaults to "
"`~/.local/share`. `bash` and `fish` read those locations on their own; `zsh` "
"needs the site-functions directory on its `fpath`. Uninstalling the package "
"takes the links away. (:issue:`1604`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:375
msgid ""
"Add `pipx reset`, which uninstalls every pipx-managed package and removes "
"the shared libraries, the caches, the standalone interpreters, the logs and "
"the trash, so pipx starts over from a fresh install. It asks before it "
"removes anything, `--yes` answers for a script, and `--dry-run` lists what "
"would go. (:issue:`1606`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:378
msgid "Add Python interpreter arguments to `pipx run`. (:issue:`1613`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:379
msgid ""
"Add commands to hide and restore resources exposed from an environment. (:"
"issue:`1645`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:380
msgid "Install the generated pipx manual page from wheels. (:issue:`1657`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:381
msgid "Add `pipx cache` and `pipx run --refresh`. (:issue:`1681`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:382
msgid "Add `--include-apps-from` for selected dependencies. (:issue:`1725`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:383
msgid ""
"Add `pipx exec ENVIRONMENT APPLICATION` for installed environments. (:issue:"
"`1726`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:384
msgid "Support injecting extras into a main package. (:issue:`1805`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:385
msgid "Install from PEP 751 lock files. (:issue:`1807`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:386
msgid "Add dependency cooldowns. (:issue:`1811`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:387
msgid ""
"Validate requested apps and restore prior environments on failure. (:issue:"
"`1908`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:388
msgid ""
"Default `PIPX_HOME` to the platform data directory on macOS and Windows "
"again, which restores `~/Library/Application Support/pipx` on macOS. "
"`platformdirs` reads `XDG_DATA_HOME` and `XDG_CACHE_HOME` on macOS, so "
"exporting those moves the pipx directories. A pipx home from an earlier "
"release keeps working as a fallback. (:issue:`1946`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:391
msgid ""
"Group the manifest commands under `pipx manifest`: use `pipx manifest lock` "
"and `pipx manifest sync` in place of the top-level `pipx lock` and `pipx "
"sync`. Keeping both verbs under one noun matches `pipx cache` and `pipx "
"interpreter` and leaves the top-level command list about the manifest rather "
"than two loose verbs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:394
msgid ""
"Keep `--json` only on `pipx list`, where it prints the versioned package "
"snapshot that `install-all` reads back. Every other command dropped the `--"
"json` alias in favour of `--output json`, so the snapshot format and the "
"result envelope no longer share a flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:397
msgid ""
"Name the existing-environment argument `ENVIRONMENT` across `inject`, "
"`uninject`, `expose`, `unexpose`, `pin`, `unpin`, `uninstall`, `reinstall`, "
"and `exec`, and fix the `uninject` help, which described the argument as the "
"environment to inject into rather than uninject from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:400
msgid ""
"Record the interpreter and backend in the structured `install`, `upgrade`, "
"and `upgrade-all` results, list `PIPX_GLOBAL_COMPLETION_DIR` in `pipx "
"environment`, and show the shell-completion directory in `pipx list`. "
"Completions had a global override that pipx honoured but never surfaced, and "
"the records omitted which Python and backend produced a venv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:404
msgid ""
"Rename `--include-apps-from` to `--include-resources-from` and the manifest "
"key to match. The option always exposed manual pages and shell completions "
"alongside apps, so the new name describes what it does; `--include-apps` "
"keeps its name. A venv recorded under the old key is migrated on read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:412
msgid ""
"Check a candidate interpreter's real patch version against `requires-"
"python`. pipx matched only on the minor version, so it rejected an installed "
"`3.13.7` for `>=3.13.5` and accepted `3.14.6` for `<3.14.1`. It now queries "
"each resolved interpreter and keeps the first whose full version satisfies "
"the constraint. (:issue:`387`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:415
msgid ""
"Keep existing exposed files when copy-based environments provide the same "
"resource name. (:issue:`540`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:416
msgid ""
"Recover custom paths when pipx manages its own installation on Unix. (:issue:"
"`774`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:417
msgid ""
"Keep install failures in JSON with the correct environment. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:418
msgid ""
"Show injected apps in `pipx list` on systems that copy launchers. (:issue:"
"`997`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:419
msgid ""
"Serialize shared-library maintenance across pipx processes. (:issue:`1056`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:420
msgid ""
"Wait for an installation before listing its environment. (:issue:`1056`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:421
msgid ""
"Draw the installer progress bar while the download runs. pipx reads the "
"installer output over a pipe, which hid the terminal from `pip`, so `pip` "
"held its bar back and printed a finished one once the download had ended. (:"
"issue:`1069`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:423
msgid ""
"Preserve symlinks in `PIPX_HOME` when creating environments. (:issue:`1327`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:424
msgid "Create Windows launchers for PEP 723 scripts. (:issue:`1388`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:425
msgid ""
"Preserve the terminal encoding for applications started by `pipx run`. (:"
"issue:`1423`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:426
msgid ""
"Make `ensurepath --global` update the system PATH configuration instead of "
"root's shell profiles. (:issue:`1452`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:427
msgid ""
"Refresh `pipx_metadata.json` after `pipx runpip ... install` replaces the "
"main package, so future `upgrade` and `reinstall` commands stop following a "
"stale editable source path. (:issue:`1473`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:429
msgid ""
"Accept bare local Git and Mercurial URLs such as `git+file:///path/to/"
"repository@revision`. (:issue:`1583`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:430
msgid "Recreate the shared environment when pip cannot run. (:issue:`1606`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:431
msgid ""
"Resolve local `--find-links` paths before pipx changes the working "
"directory. (:issue:`1637`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:432
msgid ""
"Keep pipx startup usable when locked files prevent trash cleanup. (:issue:"
"`1847`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:433
msgid ""
"Fix `pipx run --with` being silently dropped for PEP 723 scripts on the pip "
"backend; the extra packages are now installed into the temporary venv. (:"
"issue:`1850`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:435
msgid ""
"Fix `pipx uninject` leaving the injected package's man page symlinks behind. "
"(:issue:`1853`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:436
msgid ""
"Preserve `--editable` when installing a local package after a non-local "
"package. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:437
msgid ""
"Emit path warnings after logging setup for the active local or global "
"context. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:438
msgid ""
"Treat empty values for pipx path environment variables as unset. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:439
msgid ""
"Apply a 30-second timeout to standalone Python index and archive network "
"requests. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:440
msgid ""
"Enforce pip's minimum supported version when shared-library upgrades include "
"a user pin. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:441
msgid ""
"Remove exposed apps that use a venv suffix when uninjecting packages. (:"
"issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:442
msgid ""
"Report corrupt venv metadata as missing without aborting list and bulk "
"commands. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:443
msgid ""
"Return user-set values for the advertised `pipx environment --value` "
"choices. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:444
msgid ""
"Keep existing venv metadata when pipx cannot write its replacement. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:445
msgid ""
"Keep trash cleanup non-fatal during directory races and failed moves. (:"
"issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:446
msgid ""
"List only packages whose pin state changed during `pipx unpin`. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:447
msgid "Reject both Windows path separators in package names. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:448
msgid ""
"Resolve relative paths in attached `-c` and `-f` pip arguments before "
"invoking pip. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:449
msgid "Support standalone Python downloads on Windows ARM64. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:450
msgid ""
"Avoid import crashes when stderr or its encoding is unavailable. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:451
msgid ""
"Keep Windows uninject working while an exposed app runs. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:452
msgid ""
"Translate pip binary and trusted-host options to valid uv run arguments, and "
"reject `--no-deps` before invoking uv. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:453
msgid ""
"Validate members before extracting a standalone Python archive on Python "
"3.10.0-3.10.11, which predate tarfile's data filter. pipx now refuses any "
"entry whose path or link target would escape the download directory instead "
"of falling back to an unfiltered extraction. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:456
msgid ""
"Return a resolution error when standalone Python lacks a build for the "
"current platform. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:457
msgid ""
"Prevent `install --force` from saving its internal `--force-reinstall` "
"option in package metadata. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:458
msgid ""
"Continue bulk interpreter upgrades after finding a corrupt standalone "
"interpreter. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:459
msgid "Skip shared-library maintenance for no-op installs. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:460
msgid ""
"Compare metadata versions by parsed release components when selecting shared "
"libraries. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:461
msgid ""
"Wait for the animation thread to stop before clearing its final frame. (:"
"issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:462
msgid ""
"Preserve standalone archive extraction on Python 3.10 releases without the "
"tar filter API. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:463
msgid ""
"Preserve noncanonical package prefixes when completing names of installed "
"virtual environments. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:464
msgid ""
"Preserve stored pip arguments for injected packages during `pipx upgrade --"
"include-injected`. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:465
msgid ""
"Preserve caller-owned pip arguments when creating the shared-library "
"environment. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:466
msgid ""
"Use tar's data filter when extracting standalone Python archives for "
"consistent safety. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:467
msgid ""
"Skip cache tag files when removing expired `pipx run` environments. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:468
msgid "Allow forced installs in existing uv environments. (:issue:`1924`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:469
msgid ""
"Store the venv cache and the logs in the platform cache and log directories "
"on every platform, and keep them out of a pipx home that only exists for "
"backwards compatibility. Setting `PIPX_HOME` still keeps both inside it. (:"
"issue:`1946`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:471
msgid ""
"Retry fetching a standalone Python build when GitHub's release CDN returns a "
"transient error, so a momentary `5xx` or rate-limit response no longer fails "
"the install. (:issue:`1960`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:473
msgid ""
"Apply `pipx manifest lock` as all-or-nothing. When a manifest declares locks "
"for several tools, pipx wrote the regenerated files one at a time, so a "
"failure partway left some locks new and others old. Each target is now "
"backed up before it is replaced and every applied lock is rolled back if any "
"replacement fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:476
msgid ""
"Apply a 30-second timeout and a 10 MiB size limit when downloading a remote "
"`pipx run` or `pipx install` script, so a stalled or oversized URL can no "
"longer hang pipx or exhaust memory. `pipx run` also accepts a script URL "
"with a query string, such as `tool.py?raw=1`, by matching on the URL path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:479
msgid ""
"Gate a PyPI release on the test suite and validate the built artifacts "
"before publishing. The release workflow now runs the full test matrix for "
"the tagged commit, checks the distributions with `twine`, and confirms the "
"built version matches the tag, so a broken build or a mismatched tag cannot "
"reach PyPI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:482
msgid ""
"Honour a script's PEP 723 `requires-python` on the pip-backed `pipx run`. "
"Without an explicit `--python`, pipx now picks an interpreter that satisfies "
"the constraint, matching what the uv backend already does; with an explicit "
"`--python` that fails the constraint it reports a clear error instead of "
"running on an unsupported interpreter. A malformed inline metadata block now "
"produces a readable message rather than a traceback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:486
msgid ""
"Include `pipx run --with` packages in the run-cache key. Because they were "
"absent, `pipx run TOOL` and `pipx run --with EXTRA TOOL` shared one cached "
"environment, so extras injected by one invocation leaked into later runs "
"that asked for none. Each distinct set of extras now gets its own "
"environment, and the extras are injected only when that environment is first "
"built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:490
msgid ""
"Keep the backups that `install --force` and `reinstall` take while replacing "
"an environment in pipx's trash rather than beside the live environments. A "
"backup placed in the venvs directory was picked up as a broken environment "
"by a concurrent `list` or `reinstall-all`; the trash shares the home's "
"filesystem, so restoring a backup is still an atomic rename."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:494
msgid ""
"Make a standalone Python upgrade atomic. pipx used to delete the existing "
"interpreter before downloading its replacement, so a failed download or "
"unpack left no interpreter at all. The new build is now staged beside the "
"old one and swapped in only once it is complete, and a failed swap restores "
"the previous build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:497
msgid ""
"Make the expired-cache sweep that runs before `pipx run` non-blocking. pipx "
"used to wait for a lock on every other cached environment, so a concurrent "
"`pipx run` whose install held one of those locks stalled the new run, a "
"stall that lasted the whole install on Windows. The sweep now skips any "
"environment another run is holding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:500
msgid ""
"Probe a `uv` found on `PATH` before using it, and bound every `uv --version` "
"call with a timeout. A broken or hanging `uv` on `PATH` previously slipped "
"past discovery and stalled the next command; pipx now skips such a binary "
"and reports a clear error instead of hanging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:503
msgid ""
"Reject a `--suffix` that contains anything but letters, digits, and the "
"characters `.` `_` `-` `+` `@`. A suffix is spliced straight into the names "
"of the links pipx writes into `PIPX_BIN_DIR` and `PIPX_MAN_DIR`, so a value "
"such as `/../../owned` could previously place those links outside pipx's own "
"directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:506
msgid ""
"Remove a dropped app or man page during upgrade only when pipx still owns "
"the exposed file, so a command a user or another package replaced is left in "
"place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:508
msgid ""
"Report `pipx expose` as a partial or failed operation when a resource cannot "
"be linked because a foreign file already occupies its target name. The "
"command previously claimed success while silently leaving those apps or "
"manual pages unexposed; it now lists each conflict in the structured result "
"and exits non-zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:511
msgid ""
"Stop forcing `UV_NO_PROGRESS=1` on every uv call. The override silenced uv's "
"progress bar even when pipx asked to draw one, and it ignored a "
"`UV_NO_PROGRESS` already set in the environment. pipx now suppresses the bar "
"only in quiet, JSON, and non-interactive runs, and defers to the caller's "
"`UV_NO_PROGRESS` when it does want progress shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:514
msgid ""
"Track exposed shell completions through the full environment lifecycle. "
"Stale-resource cleanup during install, upgrade, and reinstall, the repair "
"relink check, and the ownership filter now include completions alongside "
"apps and manual pages, so a completion a package stops shipping is removed "
"instead of lingering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:520
msgid "Performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:522
msgid ""
"Check upgrades in parallel and skip installs for current packages. (:issue:"
"`1353`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:523
msgid ""
"Index installed distributions during environment inspection. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:524
msgid "Cache each managed environment's site-packages path. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:525
msgid "Read environment metadata once per interpreter upgrade. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:526
msgid ""
"Cache shared-library validity checks within each pipx process. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:527
msgid ""
"List managed environments only when shell completion requests them. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:528
msgid "Cache resolved pipx context paths. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:529
