"Compute only the requested `pipx environment --value` entry. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:530
msgid ""
"Reuse the `pipx run` PATH lookup when warning about an existing app. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:531
msgid ""
"Resolve the default Python interpreter on first use instead of import. (:"
"issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:532
msgid ""
"Inspect legacy environments once during uninstall and reinstall. (:issue:"
"`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:538
msgid ""
"Document the pipx application scope and feature boundaries. (:issue:`177`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:542 ../../../changelog.rst:648
#: ../../../changelog.rst:904 ../../../changelog.rst:1046
msgid "Deprecations and Removals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:544
msgid ""
"Remove the `PIPX_HOME_ALLOW_SPACE` environment variable and the warning "
"about spaces in the pipx home path. `pip` and `uv` both write a `/bin/sh` "
"wrapper as the shebang when the interpreter path contains a space, so "
"applications installed into such a path run. (:issue:`1946`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:550
msgid "`1.15.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.15.0>`_ - 2026-06-24"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:555
msgid ""
"Add a ``--dry-run`` flag to ``pipx ensurepath`` that reports which "
"directories would be added to ``PATH`` without modifying ``PATH`` or any "
"shell configuration file. (:issue:`1014`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:561
msgid ""
"Fix ``pipx uninject`` for uv-backed environments, where uv lacks pip's "
"``list --not-required`` option. Both backends now derive the not-required "
"set from installed distribution metadata, so they behave identically, and a "
"dependency pulled in only by another package's extra is kept instead of "
"being treated as removable. (:issue:`1841`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:566
msgid "`1.14.1 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.14.1>`_ - 2026-06-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:571
msgid ""
"Restore the original package if ``pipx reinstall-all`` is interrupted during "
"reinstall. (:issue:`966`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:572
msgid "Allow importing ``pipx.util`` before ``pipx.paths``. (:issue:`1333`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:573
msgid ""
"Ensure ``pipx inject --force`` reinstalls injected packages without "
"persisting the force-reinstall option in package metadata. (:issue:`1545`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:575
msgid ""
"Preserve installer errors when package-name detection fails during local "
"package installs. (:issue:`1567`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:576
msgid ""
"Expose manual pages for editable local package installs. (:issue:`1793`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:577
msgid ""
"Fixed ``pipx pin <app> --injected-only`` so it can pin injected packages "
"when the main app is already pinned. (:issue:`1835`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:581
msgid "`1.14.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.14.0>`_ - 2026-06-04"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:586
msgid ""
"Add ``--no-path-check`` to ``pipx run`` to skip the warning when the app is "
"already on ``PATH``. Useful for shim scripts that wrap ``pipx run <app>`` "
"under the same name as the app. (:issue:`1824`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:592
msgid ""
"Add regression coverage for ``pipx inject`` accepting ``--force`` before or "
"after injected dependencies. (:issue:`1444`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:598
msgid ""
"Use the bootstrap pipx executable when adding PATH in self-managed installs. "
"(:issue:`1481`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:601
msgid "`1.13.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.13.0>`_ - 2026-05-30"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:606
msgid ""
"Add ``PIPX_DISABLE_SHARED_LIBS_AUTO_UPGRADE`` to skip automatic shared "
"library upgrades. (:issue:`1650`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:607
msgid ""
"Update the error message in get-pipx.py; it is obsoleted, not deprecated. (:"
"issue:`1813`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:612
msgid ""
"Install app scripts with shebangs that ignore ``PYTHONPATH``. (:issue:`1584`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:613
msgid ""
"Refresh cached standalone Python indexes written by older pipx versions "
"before using ``--fetch-missing-python``. (:issue:`1774`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:619
msgid "Document how to clear cache warnings from ``runpip``. (:issue:`1802`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:622
msgid "`1.12.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.12.0>`_ - 2026-05-06"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:627
msgid ""
"Add ``--fetch-python`` and ``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON`` to control standalone "
"Python downloads, with values ``always``, ``missing``, or ``never``. (:issue:"
"`1663`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:629
msgid ""
"Add an opt-in ``uv`` backend. Install ``pipx[uv]`` (or put ``uv`` on "
"``PATH``) and pipx will create venvs with ``uv venv``, manage packages with "
"``uv pip``, and run ephemeral apps via ``uv tool run``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:632
msgid ""
"**Default change:** when ``uv`` is reachable, pipx uses it for **new** venvs "
"by default. Existing venvs keep their recorded backend; flipping a venv "
"requires ``pipx reinstall NAME --backend X``. Set "
"``PIPX_DEFAULT_BACKEND=pip`` to force pip even when uv is available, or pass "
"``--backend pip`` per command. ``pipx install pip`` always picks the pip "
"backend (uv venvs have no pip)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:637
msgid ""
"Selection precedence: ``--backend`` > recorded venv metadata > "
"``PIPX_DEFAULT_BACKEND`` > auto-detect. The env var sits *below* metadata so "
"setting ``PIPX_DEFAULT_BACKEND=uv`` does not silently retarget existing pip-"
"backed venvs; the recorded backend wins until you flip it explicitly. ``pipx "
"environment`` exposes the resolved backend and its source as "
"``PIPX_RESOLVED_BACKEND`` and ``PIPX_BACKEND_SOURCE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:642
msgid ""
"**Metadata version bump:** the venv metadata file format moves from ``0.5`` "
"to ``0.6`` to record the chosen backend. Running this pipx version against "
"an existing venv rewrites its metadata to ``0.6`` on the next install/"
"upgrade. If you downgrade pipx after that, the older version raises "
"``Unknown metadata version 0.6`` and you'll need to reinstall the affected "
"venvs from the older pipx (``pipx reinstall NAME``). (:issue:`1808`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:650
msgid ""
"Deprecate ``--fetch-missing-python`` and ``PIPX_FETCH_MISSING_PYTHON``; both "
"are now aliases for ``--fetch-python=missing`` / "
"``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON=missing``. ``PIPX_FETCH_MISSING_PYTHON=0`` (and other "
"falsy values) now disables fetching, where previously any value enabled it. "
"The ``pipx.interpreter.find_python_interpreter`` keyword "
"``fetch_missing_python: bool`` is replaced by ``fetch_python: "
"FetchPythonOptions``. (:issue:`1663`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:656
msgid "`1.11.2 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.11.2>`_ - 2026-05-05"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:661
msgid ""
"Add ``pipx help`` and ``pipx help <command>`` aliases for existing help "
"output. (:issue:`1535`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:662
msgid "Drop support for Python 3.9. (:issue:`1786`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:663
msgid ""
"Replace if/elif command dispatch in main.py with argparse set_defaults. (:"
"issue:`1794`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:666
msgid "`1.11.1 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.11.1>`_ - 2026-03-31"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:671
msgid ""
"Ignore ``PIP_TARGET`` environment variable to prevent pip from installing "
"outside the venv. (:issue:`735`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:672
msgid ""
"Fix ``pipx install`` failing on Windows when the username contains non-Latin "
"characters (e.g. cyrillic, Chinese). (:issue:`780`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:674
msgid ""
"Show installed version and suggest ``upgrade`` when ``install`` detects an "
"existing installation. (:issue:`795`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:675
