msgid "`0.16.1.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/0.16.1.0>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1201
msgid ""
"Introduce the ``pipx.run`` entry point group as an alternative way to "
"declare an application for ``pipx run``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1202
msgid "Fix cursor show/hide to work with older versions of Windows. (#610)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1203
msgid "Support text colors on Windows. (#612)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1204
msgid ""
"Better platform unicode detection to avoid errors and allow showing emojis "
"when possible. (#614)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1205
msgid ""
"Don't emit show cursor or hide cursor codes if STDERR is not a tty. (#620)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1206
msgid "Sped up ``pipx list`` (#624)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1207
msgid ""
"pip errors no longer stream to the shell when pip fails during a pipx "
"install. pip's output is now saved to a log file. In the shell, pipx will "
"tell you the location of the log file and attempt to summarize why pip "
"failed. (#625)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1209
msgid ""
"For ``reinstall-all``, fixed bug where missing python executable would cause "
"error. (#634)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1210
msgid ""
"Fix regression which prevented pipx from working with pythonloc (and "
"``__pypackages__`` folder). (#636)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1213
msgid "`0.16.0.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/0.16.0.0>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1215
msgid ""
"New venv inspection! The code that pipx uses to examine and determine "
"metadata in an installed venv has been made faster, better, and more "
"reliable. It now uses modern python libraries like ``packaging`` and "
"``importlib.metadata`` to examine installed venvs. It also now properly "
"handles installed package extras. In addition, some problems pipx has had "
"with certain characters (like periods) in package names should be remedied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1219
msgid "Added reinstall command for reinstalling a single venv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1220
msgid ""
"Changed ``pipx run`` on non-Windows systems to actually replace pipx process "
"with the app process instead of running it as a subprocess. (Now using "
"python's ``os.exec*``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1222
msgid ""
"[bugfix] Fixed bug with reinstall-all command when package have been "
"installed using a specifier. Now the initial specifier is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1224
msgid ""
"[bugfix] Override display of ``PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON`` value when generating "
"web documentation for ``pipx install`` #523"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1225
msgid "[bugfix] Wrap help documentation for environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1226
msgid ""
"[bugfix] Fixed uninstall crash that could happen on Windows for certain "
"packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1227
msgid ""
"[feature] Venv package name arguments now do not have to match exactly as "
"pipx has them stored, but can be specified in any python-package-name-"
"equivalent way. (i.e. case does not matter, and ``.``, ``-``, ``_`` "
"characters are interchangeable.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1230
msgid ""
"[change] Venvs with a suffix: A suffix can contain any characters, but for "
"purposes of uniqueness, python package name rules apply--upper- and lower-"
"case letters are equivalent, and any number of ``.``, ``-``, or ``_`` "
"characters in a row are equivalent. (e.g. if you have a suffixed venv "
"``pylint_1.0A`` you could not add another suffixed venv called "
"``pylint--1-0a``, as it would not be a unique name.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1234
msgid ""
"[implementation detail] Pipx shared libraries (providing pip, setuptools, "
"wheel to pipx) are no longer installed using pip arguments taken from the "
"last regular pipx install. If you need to apply pip arguments to pipx's use "
"of pip for its internal shared libraries, use ``PIP_*`` environment "
"variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1237
msgid ""
"[feature] Autocomplete for venv names is no longer restricted to an exact "
"match to the literal venv name, but will autocomplete any logically-similar "
"python package name (i.e. case does not matter, and ``.``, ``-``, ``_`` "
"characters are all equivalent.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1240
msgid ""
"pipx now reinstall its internal shared libraries when the user executes "
"``reinstall-all``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1241
msgid ""
"Made sure shell exit codes from every pipx command are correct. In the past "
"some (like from ``pipx upgrade``) were wrong. The exit code from ``pipx "
"runpip`` is now the exit code from the ``pip`` command run. The exit code "
"from ``pipx list`` will be 1 if one or more venvs have problems that need to "
"be addressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1244
msgid ""
"pipx now writes a log file for each pipx command executed to ``$PIPX_HOME/"
"logs``, typically ``~/.local/pipx/logs``. pipx keeps the most recent 10 logs "
"and deletes others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1246
msgid ""
"``pipx upgrade`` and ``pipx upgrade-all`` now have a ``--upgrade-injected`` "
"option which directs pipx to also upgrade injected packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1248
msgid ""
"``pipx list`` now detects, identifies, and suggests a remedy for venvs with "
"old-internal data (internal venv names) that need to be updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1250
msgid ""
"Added a \"Troubleshooting\" page to the pipx web documentation for common "
"problems pipx users may encounter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1251
msgid ""
"pipx error, warning, and other messages now word-wrap so words are not split "
"across lines. Their appearance is also now more consistent."
msgstr ""

